{"audio": "1corinthians-04.opus", "voice": "Davis", "duration_ms": 159333, "sentences": [{"start_ms": 0, "end_ms": 2400, "text": "1 Corinthians, Chapter Four."}, {"start_ms": 2400, "end_ms": 9067, "text": "Let a man so account of us, as of the ministers of Christ, and stewards of the mysteries of God."}, {"start_ms": 9067, "end_ms": 14267, "text": "Moreover it is required in stewards, that a man be found faithful."}, {"start_ms": 14267, "end_ms": 22000, "text": "But with me it is a very small thing that I should be judged of you, or of man's judgment: yea, I judge not mine own self."}, {"start_ms": 22000, "end_ms": 28133, "text": "For I know nothing by myself; yet am I not hereby justified: but he that judgeth me is the Lord."}, {"start_ms": 28133, "end_ms": 40667, "text": "Therefore judge nothing before the time, until the Lord come, who both will bring to light the hidden things of darkness, and will make manifest the counsels of the hearts: and then shall every man have praise of God."}, {"start_ms": 40667, "end_ms": 53467, "text": "And these things, brethren, I have in a figure transferred to myself and to Apollos for your sakes; that ye might learn in us not to think of men above that which is written, that no one of you be puffed up for one against another."}, {"start_ms": 53467, "end_ms": 55867, "text": "For who maketh thee to differ from another?"}, {"start_ms": 55867, "end_ms": 58667, "text": "and what hast thou that thou didst not receive?"}, {"start_ms": 58667, "end_ms": 64667, "text": "now if thou didst receive it, why dost thou glory, as if thou hadst not received it?"}, {"start_ms": 64667, "end_ms": 73067, "text": "Now ye are full, now ye are rich, ye have reigned as kings without us: and I would to God ye did reign, that we also might reign with you."}, {"start_ms": 73067, "end_ms": 82000, "text": "For I think that God hath set forth us the apostles last, as it were appointed to death: for we are made a spectacle unto the world, and to angels, and to men."}, {"start_ms": 82000, "end_ms": 90000, "text": "We are fools for Christ's sake, but ye are wise in Christ; we are weak, but ye are strong; ye are honourable, but we are despised."}, {"start_ms": 90000, "end_ms": 108400, "text": "Even unto this present hour we both hunger, and thirst, and are naked, and are buffeted, and have no certain dwellingplace; And labour, working with our own hands: being reviled, we bless; being persecuted, we suffer it: Being defamed, we intreat: we are made as the filth of the world,"}, {"start_ms": 108400, "end_ms": 111600, "text": "and are the offscouring of all things unto this day."}, {"start_ms": 111600, "end_ms": 116533, "text": "I write not these things to shame you, but as my beloved sons I warn you."}, {"start_ms": 116533, "end_ms": 124667, "text": "For though ye have ten thousand instructors in Christ, yet have ye not many fathers: for in Christ Jesus I have begotten you through the gospel."}, {"start_ms": 124667, "end_ms": 128133, "text": "Wherefore I beseech you, be ye followers of me."}, {"start_ms": 128133, "end_ms": 140267, "text": "For this cause have I sent unto you Timotheus, who is my beloved son, and faithful in the Lord, who shall bring you into remembrance of my ways which be in Christ, as I teach every where in every church."}, {"start_ms": 140267, "end_ms": 143467, "text": "Now some are puffed up, as though I would not come to you."}, {"start_ms": 143467, "end_ms": 150400, "text": "But I will come to you shortly, if the Lord will, and will know, not the speech of them which are puffed up, but the power."}, {"start_ms": 150400, "end_ms": 153600, "text": "For the kingdom of God is not in word, but in power."}, {"start_ms": 153600, "end_ms": 154533, "text": "What will ye?"}, {"start_ms": 154533, "end_ms": 159333, "text": "shall I come unto you with a rod, or in love, and in the spirit of meekness?"}], "words": [{"t": "1", "s": 0, "e": 726, "si": 0}, {"t": "Corinthians,", "s": 726, "e": 1331, "si": 0}, {"t": "Chap